  "kind": "zone4",
  "name": "W3 · Steep slope under Blackbutt (draft)",
  "notes": "Job: most of the hillside – steep (mostly 29–38°), sandy acidic soil, rain shadow under the Blackbutt. Managed bush and timber, Zone 4.\nTimber 8–10 m apart: silky oak, hoop pine, crow's ash, red cedar scattered, spotted gum on the driest spurs, yellowwood pollarded.\nMiddle: feijoa and grumichama. Ground: midyim, native ginger, pinto peanut below the basins.\nAvocado (moved from the SE goat trial): only a few, in the sunniest gaps and on spurs, each on a mound or bench below a half-moon basin, never in a wet hollow. Rule of five: plant five, see which spots win. Keep goats out of any pocket with avocados.\nChop-and-drop, pushing material downhill onto the contour; a small half-moon basin at each planting.\nNot here: walnut, olive or mango under the canopy. Keep the existing Blackbutt.\nPlaced from the 2022 LiDAR (1 m): slope, flow lines and ground light.\nDraft from the 19–20 Oct western high edge plan – adjust on site.",
